WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-02 - Periapsis (Closest Approach)
NOTE Artist: The Stardust Engine
NOTE Album: Sanctuary (Zero-G) (2003)

00:00:03.216 --> 00:00:09.500
Welcome to the Engine Room Records Planetarium and our presentation of Sanctuary.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:16.500
Having established our initial tidal lock, our trajectory now brings us to the periapsis.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:28.500
This is the point in our orbit closest to the parent body, where gravitational pull is strongest and our velocity reaches its absolute maximum.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:34.657
Please remain seated as we initiate the orbital slingshot maneuver.

00:00:34.657 --> 00:01:04.428
[Instrumental Intro — High-Speed 16th-Note Analog Sequencer & Quantized Drum Machine]

00:01:04.428 --> 00:01:08.000
The shadow grows, the planet swells

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.951
I'm dropping down the gravity wells

00:01:12.011 --> 00:01:15.500
But I'm not here to crash and burn

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.000
I'm riding on the massive turn

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.435
The telemetry is spinning wild

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.500
But my trajectory is perfectly dialed

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.200
The sequencer is running hot

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.813
I'm lining up the perfect shot

00:01:33.913 --> 00:01:37.500
A hundred thousand miles an hour

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.500
Stealing all the giant's power!

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.200
Periapsis! Cutting through the zone

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.921
Flying faster than I've ever known

00:01:49.021 --> 00:01:52.800
Closest approach, scraping the sky

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.800
Using the pull just to watch it fly by

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.200
We're taking the momentum and breaking the route

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.500
Periapsis! Riding the slingshot out!

00:02:10.068 --> 00:02:13.800
The atmosphere is brushing the glass

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.500
A blur of violet as I pass

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.000
I feel the friction start to heat

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.498
But I am perfectly on the beat

00:02:24.538 --> 00:02:28.260
They thought the gravity would hold me down

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:32.200
But I'm just using it to leave this town

